'' THE FUNCTION NAME IN AN -exx ABORT. fb_ErrorSetFuncName is what makes fbc's
'' 'oob.bas::TOUCHIT()' where this used to print 'oob.bas()'.
''
'' SAVE AND RESTORE, because the name is GLOBAL STATE: fbc keeps the previous value in a
'' local and puts it back on the way out, so a returned-from procedure does not leave its
'' name behind for everything after it. That is why each name appears TWICE -- once set
'' on entry, once restored before the ret.
''
'' -exx ONLY. Measured across the family: '-e', '-ex' and no flag emit none of this.
'' boundchk-off.test is the same shape for the checks themselves.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -exx --emit-ir tests/codegen/src/errfuncname.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: declare ptr @"fb_ErrorSetFuncName"
'' EXPECT-OUT: declare ptr @"fb_ErrorSetModName"
'' THE SOURCE NAME, UPPERCASED, and not the mangled one: fbc's abort says TOUCHIT.
'' EXPECT-OUT: TOUCHIT
